<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tz'utujil people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tz'utujils, Tzutujil</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tz'utujil are a Maya people living around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-atitlan">Lake Atitlán</a> in the highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>. From the 13th century they formed a kingdom with its capital at Chuitinamit near present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> Atitlán, controlling the lake shores and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cacao">cacao</a> lands on the Pacific slope, and fought the K'iche' and Kaqchikel. In 1524 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-alvarado">Pedro de Alvarado</a>, aided by Kaqchikel allies, defeated them. The Tz'utujil language is still spoken in towns around the lake.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tzutujil-people.jpg" alt="Tz'utujil people" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: chensiyuan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Santiago_de_atitlan_natives_2009.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
